<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission silent on OECD forecasts.</title>
<headline>EU Commission silent on OECD forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission refused to comment on Thursday about OECD forecasts showing France, Germany and Italy all falling short of qualifying for economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission does not comment on other people's forecasts,&quot; a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development predicted that the three countries would all have deficit to gross domestic product ratios of 3.2 percent this year, as against EMU's 3.0 percent target.</p>
<p>The Commission, whose forecasts will be used when it comes time to judge qualification for the single currency, is projecting France and Germany to have deficit/GDP ratios of 3.0 percent with Italy at 3.2 percent.</p>
</text>
